            <div xml:id="d129-a6">

                <pb facs="0245" n="149" xml:id="pg149"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to the Tsungli Yamen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness and Your Excellencies</hi>: I have the
                    honor to bring to the attention of your highness and your excellencies the fact
                    that the situation at Paoting Fu is very threatening, and as there are many
                    American missionaries there I request that telegraphic instructions be sent to
                    the high authorities there to take stringent measures to protect them and
                    prevent any trouble. It is important that prompt and efficient action be taken
                    at once.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
